! Hasenheide apartment experiments, run Hep_160_S1_R2 (fire series Hep_160_150).
! Adapted from fds_decks/hep_160_150_ysmatched.fds of the reproduction package openbcl/hasenheide1-reproduction v1.0.0
! (Zenodo doi:10.5281/zenodo.24054120). Changes for the Validation Guide: CHID; HUMIDITY, P_INF and TMPA
! measured before this run (results/measurement/timeseries/runs.csv); the HRR ramp of this
! run, from its load-cell mass with the chain of scripts/reduce_hrr_from_mass.py, thinned to
! 0.2 kW and rescaled to the fuel energy; HEAT_OF_COMBUSTION 44.0 MJ/kg, the net heat of combustion
! of the liquid fuel for complete combustion, with IDEAL=T (instead of the measured effective
! 41.345 MJ/kg), and the ramp uses the effective
! value FDS derives from it, 42.667 MJ/kg, so the fuel and soot mass rates are the measured ones;
! the decay of the pan surface temperature (RAMP_T) starts at the burning duration of this run; the
! line-of-sight beams output TRANSMISSIVITY (%/m) instead of PATH OBSCURATION (%), only for
! the LEM beams used in the Guide, plus EXTINCTION COEFFICIENT (1/m) on the same paths, with
! the free-text note above the beams rewritten for that; the window HOLEs reach 1 cm beyond
! the mesh boundary, and the note on the former window vents is removed; outputs reduced to
! the thermocouple trees in F1 and F2 and the LEM beams, and 4 slices along the flow path
! (no smoke detectors, boundary, restart or mass files); output every T_END/NFRAMES = 10 s,
! the devices averaged over that interval.


&HEAD CHID='Hasenheide_Hep_160_S1_R2', TITLE='Leipzig Hasenheide - Light Extinction in Fire Smoke'/
&TIME T_END=1200.0/
&DUMP NFRAMES=120/
&MISC HUMIDITY=70.7, P_INF=99312, TMPA=12.71, SIMULATION_MODE='LES'/

&MESH ID='Near-Field-01', IJK=54,50,20, XB=1.4,2.75,1.5,2.75,0.0,0.5, MPI_PROCESS=0/
